# OpenAPI Schema Editing Patterns

## Required Fields Pattern

Always specify required fields explicitly:

```yaml
# ✅ CORRECT: Explicit required array
type: object
required:
  - id
  - name
  - email
properties:
  id:
    type: string
  name:
    type: string
  email:
    type: string
  phoneNumber:
    type: string
    nullable: true  # Optional field

# ❌ WRONG: No required array
type: object
properties:
  id:
    type: string
  name:
    type: string
```

## Nullable vs Optional

- **Optional field**: Not in `required` array
- **Nullable field**: Can be `null`, use `nullable: true`

```yaml
# ✅ CORRECT: Clear nullable pattern
properties:
  middleName:
    type: string
    nullable: true
    description: Optional middle name (can be null)

  lastName:
    type: string
    description: Required last name (not nullable)
```

## Descriptions

Add descriptions for non-obvious fields:

```yaml
# ✅ CORRECT: Descriptive
properties:
  status:
    type: string
    enum: [pending, approved, rejected]
    description: Current approval status of the application

  createdAt:
    type: string
    format: date-time
    description: ISO 8601 timestamp when record was created

# ❌ WRONG: Missing descriptions
properties:
  status:
    type: string
    enum: [pending, approved, rejected]
  createdAt:
    type: string
```

## Unverified Backend Contracts

Mark fields that need backend verification with `x-unverified: true`:

```yaml
# ✅ CORRECT: Mark unverified fields
properties:
  agentCommission:
    type: number
    nullable: true
    x-unverified: true
    description: "TODO: Verify with backend - observed in responses but not documented in route handler"
```

## Enum Values

Use enums for fixed value sets:

```yaml
# ✅ CORRECT: Enum with description
status:
  type: string
  enum:
    - draft
    - pending
    - approved
    - rejected
  description: Document workflow status

# ❌ WRONG: String without enum constraint
status:
  type: string
  description: Status (draft, pending, approved, or rejected)
```

## Nested Objects

Prefer inline definitions for simple nested objects, $ref for reusable types:

```yaml
# ✅ CORRECT: Inline for simple nested object
address:
  type: object
  required:
    - street
    - city
  properties:
    street:
      type: string
    city:
      type: string

# ✅ CORRECT: $ref for reusable type
location:
  $ref: '#/components/schemas/GeoLocation'
```

## Array Properties

Always specify `items` for arrays:

```yaml
# ✅ CORRECT: Array with items
favoriteHomes:
  type: array
  items:
    type: string
  description: List of saved home IDs

# ✅ CORRECT: Array of objects
results:
  type: array
  items:
    $ref: '#/components/schemas/SearchResult'

# ❌ WRONG: Array without items
favoriteHomes:
  type: array
```

## Date/Time Fields

Use `format: date-time` for timestamps:

```yaml
# ✅ CORRECT: ISO 8601 datetime
createdAt:
  type: string
  format: date-time
  description: ISO 8601 timestamp (e.g., 2024-03-15T10:30:00Z)

# ✅ CORRECT: Date only
birthDate:
  type: string
  format: date
  description: Date in YYYY-MM-DD format
```

## Response Objects

Follow consistent response patterns:

```yaml
# ✅ CORRECT: Response object pattern
UserProfileResponse:
  type: object
  required:
    - user
  properties:
    user:
      $ref: '#/components/schemas/UserProfile'
    metadata:
      type: object
      properties:
        lastUpdated:
          type: string
          format: date-time
```

## Validation After Changes

After editing any schema file:

```bash
# 1. Validate OpenAPI spec
swagger-cli validate openapi/openapi.yaml

# 2. Regenerate client types
cd Client && pnpm generate:api-types

# 3. Regenerate server schemas
cd Server && bash scripts/generate-pydantic-models.sh

# 4. Type check
cd Client && pnpm typecheck
```

## Common Mistakes

```yaml
# ❌ WRONG: Missing type
properties:
  name:
    description: User's name

# ✅ CORRECT: Always specify type
properties:
  name:
    type: string
    description: User's name

# ❌ WRONG: Using null as type
properties:
  optional:
    type: null

# ✅ CORRECT: Use nullable
properties:
  optional:
    type: string
    nullable: true
```

## Quick Checklist

When editing a schema file:

- [ ] `type` specified for all properties
- [ ] `required` array defined for required fields
- [ ] `nullable: true` for fields that can be null
- [ ] `description` added for non-obvious fields
- [ ] `enum` used for fixed value sets
- [ ] `items` specified for arrays
- [ ] `format` used for dates/times
- [ ] Validated with `swagger-cli validate`
- [ ] Types regenerated for client and server
